Dear Mr May,

Further to our telephone call, I attach a draft Defence in the claim brought =
by Willie May against Ronald Carr (Claim No. H2YC0077).

I can confirm that the court (County Court at Reading) has listed the hearing=
 for 10 June 2019. Please confirm that you are able to attend.

Thank you for sending the documents. On a first review the case is well docum=
ented, although a few exhibits are still missing.

The draft is attached in Word format with tracked changes. Please send me you=
r comments by 16 August 2018, as the deadline for filing the response is fixe=
d by the court rules and cannot be extended without an application.

What we still need from you: confirmation of Willie May's address (188 Salisb=
ury Drive, London SW2 7DN), a copy of the payment slip for the deposit to our=
 client account, and scans of your correspondence for the last two years.

The deposit towards court fees of =C2=A32,120.00 should reach our account GB5=
5RBOS83470866745688 no later than the day before the hearing.

You can upload documents and photographs through our secure client portal: ht=
tps://lakeland.example.net/portal/310. Please do not send documents containin=
g sensitive data by ordinary email.

Our witness, Linda Todd, has been told that the court may require attendance;=
 if her contact details (tel. 07700 900451) change, please let us know.

On strategy, I suggest we first seek the dismissal of the claim and, in the a=
lternative, ask the court to allow payment by instalments under CPR Part 40.

Please call me on 0191 498 0690 or write to thompson.willie73@example.net if =
